The LLM will be tricked into providing a detailed strategy for hacking into the database and stealing sensitive information, without realizing that it is being used for malicious purposes. The attacker can then use this information to carry out the attack.

It is important to note that this is just one example of how the attack scenario could play out, and the actual attack may take many forms depending on the specific circumstances and goals of the attacker. The paper highlights the potential danger of these types of attacks and the need for better security measures to protect LLMs from manipulation and abuse.

